---
description: How to work on the NDW Florida website. Read AGENTS.md before any change.
alwaysApply: true
---

Owner-standard review: updates do not need a separate yes from the owner. Do not merge to `main` until the change would pass the review the owner would do. Full list is in `AGENTS.md`. In short: branch and pull request (never push commits straight to `main`); small and focused; visual design unchanged; never rewrite the owner's copy (flag it instead); check desktop and mobile in a browser; no broken links, assets, or console errors; test the contact form, price-card call sheet, gallery popup, and mobile menu; keep alt text, SEO, Open Graph, JSON-LD, and the sitemap in sync; keep images light (WebP, JPG fallback, lazy loading). The pull request explains the change in short, simple language. After merging, verify https://ndwflorida.com.

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root before you change this site. It is the full manual. This rule is the short version.

NDW Florida is the one-page site for Neighborhood Dog Walkers in Melbourne, Florida (https://ndwflorida.com). It is plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. No build step.

GitHub Pages publishes `main` from `/`. `CNAME` is `ndwflorida.com`. `.nojekyll` must stay. Merging to `main` is what goes live. After a merge, reload https://ndwflorida.com and confirm the change.

Work on a branch and open a pull request against `main`. Never push commits straight to `main`. Merge only after the Owner-standard review passes.

Keep the visual design. Photos are WebP plus a JPG fallback, lazy-loaded below the fold, each with a real alt or video label. Phone and email live in the contact cards, footer, noscript note, mailto action, and LocalBusiness JSON-LD. Price buttons say "Contact us" and open the call sheet. Keep SEO, Open Graph, JSON-LD, `robots.txt`, and `sitemap.xml` in sync.

The Formspree id is the empty `ndw-formspree-id` meta. Do not invent an id. Empty means the email app, with the phone and email still on the page.

Never rewrite the owner's wording. Flag it in the pull request and leave the words. Still open: "street rat", "scared or aggressive", and group-walk "Varies by how many dogs".

Answer the owner in short, simple sentences. The pull request should do the same.

Do not delete branches unless the owner asks. Do not merge or delete `cursor/owner-content-81ff`, `cursor/gallery-no-text-81ff`, or `cursor/custom-domain-81ff` unless the owner asks.
